<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<robot name="IST_robot">
  <!--
SI units: m, kg, rad. Original assembly zero pose, exact SolidWorks coordinate systems.
Two fixed-ring 9/9/27 stages: carrier angles = motor/4 and motor/16.
Planet joint angles are RELATIVE to carriers: -3*motor/4 and -3*motor/16.
The stage-2 sun is part of carrier_1. The motor casing remains on base_link.
Slider and both flapping pivots are supported by base_link, not rotating carriers.
13-tooth flapping pinion: module 0.3 mm, pitch radius 1.95 mm.
Scotch yoke: slider = -0.0027*sin(motor/16). Standard URDF cannot encode
this nonlinear closure; load IST_robot.xml in MuJoCo for coupled physics.
Feathering has no actuator or mimic. User corrected stops to +/-26.1 deg, no spring
or elastic return. Damping and effort/velocity limits are provisional model settings.
Material inertials: solid CNC PEEK mechanisms, PET wing frames, 10 um Kapton films.
See ../materials.json and ../recalculate_inertials.py; base_link is unchanged.
Original CAD density 1000 kg/m3 is inferred from mesh volumes, not measured.
Motor rotor inertia and aerodynamic data are not measured.
Membrane mass is integrated once; reverse visual faces add no extra mass.
Collision meshes describe geometry only; convex mesh collision is unsuitable for
gear engagement. The MJCF uses ideal gear constraints and disables mesh contacts.
-->
  <link name="base_link">
